WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.730
Stranger Things 2 has officially arrived and
has introduced two new kids to the Hawkins,

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.730
Indiana crew.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.580
Billy and Max are step-siblings who've moved
from California with their parents and couldn't

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.280
be more different from one another.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.530
Billy is a loose cannon who behaves like a
bully and desperately wants to dethrone Steve

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.160
as the coolest kid in school.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.600
Meanwhile Max is a skateboarding tomboy who
proves to be a wizard at Dig Dug and catches

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.430
the attention of Dustin and Lucas just as
they prepare to face a new threat from the

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:26.550
upside-down.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.970
The actors portraying the Stranger Things
2 duo, Dacre Montgomery and Sadie Sink, are

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.590
still relatively new to show-business as well.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:37.550
But you still may recognize them from some
of these other productions...

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.840
The comedy club

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.210
Not long before the release of Stranger Things
2, Australia native Dacre Montgomery's career

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:48.239
started gaining traction with a small role
in the 2016 Australian-American horror comedy

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:52.930
Better Watch Out — a critically acclaimed,
over-the-top film chock full of teenage talent.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:57.200
The film is basically a deadlier version of
Home Alone, and let's just say that Montgomery's

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.150
character gets in over his head.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:03.120
Soon after, Montgomery also starred as Mike
in A Few Less Men — a direct sequel to the

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.260
critically panned Australian-British comedy
A Few Best Men — before earning the role

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.280
that would transform his career altogether.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.640
Morphin' time

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.250
Dacre Montgomery's biggest pre-Stranger Things
role is unquestionably that of Red Ranger

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.900
Jason Scott, the leader of the titular superheroes
in the Power Rangers reboot.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:24.310
Although he earned the lead in the pic, he'd
never seen the show or films that started

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:25.700
it all before auditioning.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.040
He told The Hollywood Reporter, "I'd love
to blame that I was on the west coast [of

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.130
Australia], in the most isolated city on the
planet, but I think Power Rangers really had

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.470
reached every corner of the earth, so I don't
know, I just missed it!"

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.670
Even so, he had no trouble adapting to all
the mighty morphin' that went down on the

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:43.320
set and even delivered the film's most iconic
line.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.140
"It's morphin' time."

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.580
On Broadway

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:53.229
Sadie Sink started acting professionally at
10 years old, after an obsession with 2006's

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:57.680
High School Musical inspired her to pursue
drama in a rural Texas community theatre.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.079
Eventually, she earned the title role in the
2012 Broadway revival of Annie, which is when

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:04.700
the ball really started rolling on her young
career.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.039
It was also then that she first met Stranger
Things' Caleb McLaughlin and Gaten Matarazzo,

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:12.090
who were starring in The Lion King and Les
Miserables at the time.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.480
As she told Vogue, "If you're a child, and
you're on Broadway, you automatically know

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.050
every other child in a production.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.730
It's a proper community.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:22.481
There's a park on 43rd Street where we would
all go to let off energy before we had to

00:02:22.481 --> 00:02:24.290
go back and perform another show."

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:28.310
Though Annie was her biggest Broadway gig,
Sink also starred alongside veteran Helen

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.180
Mirren in 2015's The Audience.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.599
TV turn

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:37.290
While hitting it big on Broadway, Sink made
her television debut in 2013 as a guest star

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.650
on FX's hit series The Americans.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:43.940
She'd later pop up in other hit series such
as Blue Bloods and The Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.470
Of course, Sink didn't merely make cameos.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:50.190
Before landing the role of Max on Stranger
Things' second season, the young actress was

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:55.099
notably featured as a main cast member on
the NBC thriller American Odyssey.

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:56.800
Breaking into the big screen

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.810
Sadie Sink made her big-screen debut in 2016's
sports drama Chuck, in which she plays the

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.600
title character's daughter, Kimberly.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.940
The boxing biopic received generally positive
reviews, and — though her role was minimal

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:10.390
— helped bolster the young star's résumé.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:15.330
Her most prominent big-screen role to date
is that of a young Lori Walls in the 2017

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.110
American biographical drama The Glass Castle.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:23.190
Based on Jeannette Walls' 2005 memoir of the
same name, the film follows an autobiographical

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:27.330
account of the author's poverty-stricken childhood
existence with her family and father.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:31.129
While the film has received mixed reviews,
it certainly proved that Sink has just as

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:34.580
much talent on a film set as she does on a
small screen series.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.970
As Stranger Things 2 escalates their public
profile, count on Dacre Montgomery and Sadie

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.879
Sink to continue accelerating their already
prolific screen careers.

00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:43.879
Thanks for watching!

